{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416064-confused-by-retainers-what-can-they-do","id":1416064,"title":"Confused by Retainers. What can they do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-29T23:54:49-07:00","id":1416064,"title":"Confused by Retainers. What can they do?","content":"So my character is Resources 5 because he makes Artifacts on commission, and therefore is ludicrously famous and wealthy. That money is more or less entirely invested in the Guild and was managed by a fellow Solar Bureacrat who left the game for story reasons and so I went and rescued a 2 dot retainer from Hell to act as my personal banker because that's how Solars be. <br /> <br /> I worked out with the ST that this woman is a Guild official who went missing a few years ago (lost her soul to Sigereth) and that she's an expert in finance and investments so she can manage my character's huge wealth. The problem is I have no idea how Retainers actually work. <br /> <br /> A 2 dot retainer has &quot;a specialty in the relevant fields&quot; and several 4 or 5 dot abilities\u2026 but not a dice pool and who knows how attributes work for her (she's entirely mortal by the way. A mundane expert). It also says they have some relevant connections and experience. <br /> <br /> So how do i actually stat out this retainer for her job? Bureacracy 5 with a Specialty in Investing seems like a given, but is she Wits 4? Wits 2? How does this work? Are there any example retainers? How many abilities am I allowed to give her? <br /> <br /> Anyway, here's what I have<br /> Retainer, the Expert Investor:<br /> <br /> Perception 2<br /> Int 3<br /> Wits 4<br /> <br /> Charisma 2<br /> Manipulate 3<br /> Appearance 3<br /> <br /> Strenght/Dex/Stam all 2. <br /> <br /> Bureaucracy 5 (Finance)<br /> Socialize 4 (Reading People)<br /> <br /> Any help would be appreciated. This is probably the most handwavy merit in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T01:20:45-07:00","id":1416077,"title":"","content":"I would straight up build the character as a Heroic Mortal PC using the rules on page 125, give the sheet to your ST along with a pencil and an eraser and never worry about it again.<br /> <br /> You don't usually roll for Bureaucracy projects, so knowing your money is being managed by someone competent is basically all you need to know. And even if you did roll, I usually just narrate NPC actions because I don't want to bog the game down.<br /> <br /> You have a skilled professional who works for you. That's a lot like having a nice colourful hat. It doesn't need stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-30-2020, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T01:26:05-07:00","id":1416078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416064-confused-by-retainers-what-can-they-do?p=1416077#post1416077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would straight up build the character as a Heroic Mortal PC using the rules on page 125, give the sheet to your ST along with a pencil and an eraser and never worry about it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Although try to make the sheet look something like you might expect from a real person. Like don't have every single merit/ability/attribute that you're going to be using her for at max, and leave everything else at zero.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also as to what she should do in practice, I do retainers like this. If there's any scene where every PC party member is present, the retainer either can't be there or will be functionally absent, barring some unique thing only she can do. Otherwise she can be sent off to do things on her own with a reasonable chance of success depending on what you're sending her off to do.<br /> <br /> Alternatively if not every PC is present in the scene, somebody who's character is missing can temporarily assume control of the retainer for something to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T01:30:19-07:00","id":1416079,"title":"","content":"I agree completely with DrLoveMonkey above there.<br /> <br /> If it helps, here's a 1-dot ally we made for my game. She is god-blooded warrior so it's not a direct translation -- I think Bureacracy 5 / Socialize 4 with Specialties is perfectly appropriate for your Retainer.<br /> <br /> (I've got a couple of young Dragon-Blooded Retainers filed somewhere too.)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Tinkara Dovak<br /> God-Blooded<br /> Warlike Princess<br /> <br /> Strength 2<br /> Dexterity 3<br /> Stamina 2<br /> <br /> Charisma 3<br /> Manipulation 3<br /> Appearance 3<br /> <br /> Perception 2<br /> Intelligence 2<br /> Wits 2<br /> <br /> Athletics 2<br /> Awareness 2 (Join Battle)<br /> Brawl 1<br /> Bureaucracy 2<br /> Integrity 2<br /> Investigation 1<br /> Linguistics 1<br /> Lore: Dovaki education 1<br /> Melee 3 (Warclub)<br /> Occult 1 (Tomonas)<br /> Performance 2<br /> Presence 3<br /> Resistance 2<br /> Socailize 2<br /> Stealth 1<br /> Survival 1<br /> War 1 (Dovaki Military)<br /> <br /> Merits (Native Language: Riverspeak)<br /> <br /> Exalted Healing<br /> Resources 3<br /> Influence (Dovaki Princess) 4<br /> Artifact (Warclub) 3<br /> High Realm<br /> Low Realm<br /> Forest-tongue<br /> Tribal Language: Dovaki<br /> Contacts 1 (Local Guild Merchants)<br /> Followers 1 (Personally loyal bureaucrats)<br /> Followers 1 (Handmaidens)<br /> <br /> Join Battle: 5<br /> Resist Poison/Disease: 4<br /> Parry: 4<br /> Evasion: 2<br /> Soak: 5 (Buff Jacket)<br /> Rush: 5<br /> Disengage: 3<br /> <br /> Warclub: Accuracy 9 (7 Decisive), Damage 14 (OVR 4), Bashing, Smashing, Melee<br /> <br /> Social: 6<br /> Read Intentions: 4<br /> Guile: 3<br /> Resolve: 2</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-30-2020, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}